      "writtenOn": "2022-10-26T18:08:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "come to think of it, if this structure was not packed there would be no need for padding, the complier would do it for us, and it would allow to generate smaller/faster code because all fields would be aligned.\n\nSomething to think about as a clean up/code size reduction measure.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 192,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 194,
        "endChar": 17
      },
      "revId": "ebfa40a8230ac6721ae0b2269f47a6b765ff6165",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "99f37f62_a5f381b4",
        "filename": "common/ap_ro_integrity_check.c",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 194,
      "author": {
        "id": 1136059
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-26T18:23:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We won\u0027t be able to change this later since we can\u0027t update the format of saved information. If we have pad[3] here and use __packed, we could add 3 more bytes of information into the same space. If we don\u0027t use __packed and remove pad[3], then any elements we add to the struct will take more space.\n\nShould I move validate_flags to the end of the struct before pad, since that\u0027s the thing that messes up the alignment?\n\nI doubt we\u0027ll ever modify this struct and there\u0027s a lot of space left in the AP RO flash space, so I\u0027m fine with either. We just need to decide now.",
      "parentUuid": "1db071ba_cfed0035",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 192,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 194,
        "endChar": 17
      },
      "revId": "ebfa40a8230ac6721ae0b2269f47a6b765ff6165",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "dcb80dd0_b4977fc2",
        "filename": "common/ap_ro_integrity_check.c",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 194,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-26T20:44:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "so maybe this is a good time to remove the packed and not worry about padding, letting the compiler do its thing, The only issue we would have to worry about is that the structure is saved in the flash at 4 byte alignment, which is guaranteed.\n\nPacking is important for data coming over the wire, which can end up unaligned in the received packet, here this is not an issue.",
      "parentUuid": "99f37f62_a5f381b4",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 192,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 194,
        "endChar": 17
