      "writtenOn": "2022-10-26T18:08:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "do we really care about this when verifying the AP RO. A much simpler information would be the range of gbb flags in the flash and the substitute value to use when calculating the hash, similar to \n\nhttps://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromiumos/platform/vboot_reference/+/3958581/7/futility/cmd_gscvd.c#468\n\nThen there is just one function calculating the hash, with a bypass for gbb flags if necessary.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 207,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 210,
        "endChar": 28
      },
      "revId": "ebfa40a8230ac6721ae0b2269f47a6b765ff6165",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "78325c06_4d85d6b7",
        "filename": "common/ap_ro_integrity_check.c",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 210,
      "author": {
        "id": 1136059
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-26T18:23:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think we need a gbbd specific ap_ro_check_header to validate the saved gbbd information and to have the possiblity of bumping the gbbd version or handling the information differently based on how it was saved later.\n\nAs far as the information included in the gbb descriptor. I\u0027m just worried we\u0027re going to overlook something. I think including the FMAP information helps us do some basic validity checks that the loaded state matches the actual ap ro information. verify_ap_ro_gbb_space just does a memcmp on the gbbd to validate it. Having the gbb and fmap information in addition doesn\u0027t add much overhead.",
      "parentUuid": "638d15f2_5bfb9e87",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 207,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 210,
        "endChar": 28
      },
      "revId": "ebfa40a8230ac6721ae0b2269f47a6b765ff6165",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bd80d02a_4af54d36",
        "filename": "common/ap_ro_integrity_check.c",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 210,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-26T20:44:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this is an unnecessary comlication of the code which verifies the signature. We sure are not planning to allow other incorrectly set fields in the verified space. It is good to be thorough when figuring out where the flags are and if they need to be tweaked when calculating the hash, but  the side calculating the hash can be much simpler.",
      "parentUuid": "78325c06_4d85d6b7",
      "range": {
